    "ex-bairds-seven-state-star-expected-update": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "thm-bairds-counterexample-off-policy-td-diverges",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let the states be $S=\\{s_1,\\ldots,s_7\\}$ and the two actions available at each state be $\\mathrm{dashed}$ and $\\mathrm{solid}$. All rewards are zero and $\\gamma=0.99$. Under $\\mathrm{dashed}$, the next state is each of $s_1,\\ldots,s_6$ with probability $1/6$; under $\\mathrm{solid}$, the next state is $s_7$ with probability $1$. The behavior policy has $b(\\mathrm{dashed}\\mid s)=6/7$ and $b(\\mathrm{solid}\\mid s)=1/7$ at every state, and the target policy selects $\\mathrm{solid}$ with probability $1$. Use the uniform state weighting $\\mu(s)=1/7$. For standard basis vectors $e_1,\\ldots,e_8$ of $\\mathbb R^8$, set $\\phi(s_i)=2e_i+e_8$ for $1\\leq i\\leq6$ and $\\phi(s_7)=e_7+2e_8$, and define $v_w(s)=\\phi(s)^\\mathsf T w$. For a behavior transition $(S,A,S')$, draw $S$ from $\\mu$, draw $A$ from $b(\\cdot\\mid S)$, and draw $S'$ from the stated action transition law. Put $\\rho=\\pi(A\\mid S)/b(A\\mid S)$ and $\\delta=\\gamma v_w(S')-v_w(S)$, and define the expected semi-gradient TD(0) update by $\\bar w^+=w+\\alpha\\,\\mathbb E_{\\mu,b}[\\rho\\delta\\,\\phi(S)]$. Also define the synchronous expected dynamic-programming update by $w^+=w+\\frac{\\alpha}{7}\\sum_{s\\in S}\\big((T^\\pi v_w)(s)-v_w(s)\\big)\\phi(s)$. For every step size $\\alpha>0$, both deterministic update sequences starting at $w_0=(1,1,1,1,1,1,10,1)$ have Euclidean norm $\\|w\\|_2=(\\sum_{i=1}^8w_i^2)^{1/2}$ tending to infinity. This is a claim about the stated expected/deterministic updates; it asserts no probability-one divergence result for individual stochastic TD trajectories.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "ex-bairds-seven-state-star-expected-update-1-1",
          "claim": "At $w_0$, every upper-state value is $2(1)+1=3$ and the seventh-state value is $10+2(1)=12$. Thus $q_u=0.99(12)-3=222/25$ and $q_7=0.99(12)-12=-3/25$. The importance ratio is $7$ on solid and $0$ on dashed; because behavior selects solid with probability $1/7$, at each fixed state the behavior-action expectation is its solid-action TD error. Uniformly averaging the seven state contributions gives increments per unit step size $2q_u/7$, $q_7/7$, and $(6q_u+2q_7)/7$: each upper feature contributes $2q_u$ to its own coordinate and $q_u$ to the common eighth coordinate, while the seventh feature contributes $q_7$ and $2q_7$ to its last two coordinates. By [F1] these values are $444/175$, $-3/175$, and $1326/175$.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "F1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "ex-bairds-seven-state-star-expected-update-2-1",
          "claim": "Multiplying these increments by $\\alpha=1/100$ gives $a_1=1+444/17500=4486/4375$, $b_1=10-3/17500=174997/17500$, and $c_1=1+1326/17500=9413/8750$, exactly as claimed; the displayed fractions give $a_1>1$ and $c_1>1$.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "step 1.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        }
      ],
